      "question": "Simplify the following expression. \\(\\frac{{12\\, - \\,6\\, \\div \\,2\\, + \\,4}}{{{3^2}\\, \\times \\,3 - 7 + 6}}\\)",
      "questionHtml": "<p>Simplify the following expression.</p>\n\n<p><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{{12\\, - \\,6\\, \\div \\,2\\, + \\,4}}{{{3^2}\\, \\times \\,3 - 7 + 6}}\\)</span></p>\n",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "\\(\\frac{{11}}{{26}}\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{{11}}{{26}}\\)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "\\(\\frac{{13}}{{18}}\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{{13}}{{18}}\\)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "\\(\\frac{{11}}{{18}}\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{{11}}{{18}}\\)</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<p><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{{12\\, - \\,6\\, \\div \\,2\\, + \\,4}}{{{3^2}\\, \\times \\,3 - 7 + 6}}\\)</span></p>\n\n<p>⇒ <span class=\"math-tex\">\\({12\\ -\\ 3\\ +\\ 4} \\over {27\\ -\\ 7\\ +\\ 6}\\)</span> =  <span class=\"math-tex\">\\({13 \\over 26}\\)</span> = <span class=\"math-tex\">\\({1 \\over 2}\\)</span></p>\n",
